      "metadata": {
        "role": "Armored investigator and anti-spell protector",
        "progression": "Custom Lineage +2 Wis; racial Fey Touched +1 Wis; Cleric 4 +2 Wis. Gauntlets replace native Str 8 with 19.",
        "grim_hollow": {
          "kind": "subclass",
          "name": "Inquisition Domain",
          "features": [
            "Witch Hunter's Strike",
            "Channel Divinity: Spell Shield",
            "Rebuke Invoker"
          ]
        },
        "import_notes": "Enter 12 gp. Apply War Caster concentration advantage manually. Spell DC 18 and AC 19 are included. Rebuke Invoker has an omitted DC in the source: default recommendation DC 16 is a declared table assumption, not printed rules. Track five Witch Hunter strikes, five Rebukes and the shared Channel Divinity pool.",
        "tactics": [
          "Use bonus-action Spell Shield before a dangerous spell exchange; its protection depends on retaining its particular temporary HP. It is a feature, so an action spell can be cast on the same turn.",
          "Against a concentrating caster, the weapon Strike adds 2d8 force and may yield temporary HP if concentration breaks. Against ordinary groups, Spirit Guardians is more efficient.",
          "Save the reaction for the most important Rebuke or War Caster opportunity spell. Rebuke deals damage; it is not an automatic Counterspell."
        ],
        "assumptions": [
          "The available Player Pack entry omits Rebuke Invoker's save DC. DC 16 is a conservative proposed ruling for this non-spell feature. The GM should settle it, including slotless leveled spellcasting; the build does not silently treat the spell DC 18 as the printed answer."
        ],
        "spell_groups": {
